<div class="container info-page">
  <header>
    <span class="info-eyebrow">Changelog</span>
    <h1 class="info-title">Site changelog</h1>
    <p class="info-lead">
      Notable changes to the site itself — not to the teachings. Newest first, and
      append-only: past entries are not rewritten.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="info-section" aria-labelledby="year-2026">
    <h2 id="year-2026">2026</h2>

    <article class="changelog-entry">
      <h3 class="changelog-date"><time datetime="2026-11-16">16 November 2026</time></h3>
      <ul class="changelog-list">
        <li><strong>One stylesheet for the whole site.</strong> Article pages used
          to carry their own CSS in every page; they now share a single cached
          style sheet, so reading a second article downloads nothing extra.</li>
        <li><strong>Faster, steadier images.</strong> WebP images are cached for a
          year, every image reserves its own space before it loads, and the largest
          gallery works now open at up to 2048&nbsp;px in the lightbox — from a
          derivative, never from the archive master.</li>
        <li><strong>Self-hosted fonts.</strong> Crimson Text and Philosopher are
          served from this domain as woff2 subsets. Google Fonts is no longer
          contacted.</li>
        <li><strong>Continuous validation.</strong> The test suite runs on every
          push again after GitHub's runner-image migration broke the browser
          install.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="changelog-entry">
      <h3 class="changelog-date"><time datetime="2026-11-15">15 November 2026</time></h3>
      <ul class="changelog-list">
        <li><strong>A social card for every article.</strong> Each article has its
          own generated 1200&times;630 card, so a shared link shows that article's
          title instead of a cropped image.</li>
        <li><strong>Feeds.</strong> <a href="/feed.xml">/feed.xml</a> carries the
          thirty most recent articles, and every topic path has its own feed.</li>
        <li><strong>Quieter measurement.</strong> Google Analytics was removed.
          Measurement moved to cookieless Cloudflare Web Analytics and Google
          Search Console; the site sets no tracking cookies.</li>
        <li><strong>Instant search results.</strong> Full-text search was kept, but
          the large article-text index now loads after the first results appear.</li>
        <li><strong>Housekeeping.</strong> Internal audit documents stopped being
          published as public pages, a stray agent-skill page was removed, and
          repository rules were written down for future contributors.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="changelog-entry">
      <h3 class="changelog-date"><time datetime="2026-10-22">22 October 2026</time></h3>
      <ul class="changelog-list">
        <li><strong>SEO and taxonomy audit.</strong> The archive, its category
          vocabulary and its Search Console coverage were reviewed; the resulting
          reports are archived in the repository and shaped the November work
          above.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="info-section" aria-labelledby="how-heading">
